    "type": "assistant_message",
    "content": "All 19 checklist items have been tested and recorded — coverage is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\n**16 PASS / 3 FAIL**\n\nCore task management is solid: creation with full details, editing, deletion, completion, active/completed views with accurate counts, priority and deadline sorting (including undated tasks sorted last), empty/whitespace title rejection, blocked-task styling and warning badges, and cycle prevention.\n\n### Failures\n\n**FT-3 — Blocked tasks can't be edited at all**\nThe requirement is that a blocked task keeps its description and priority editable while title and deadline lock. Instead the edit button is fully `disabled=true`; neither a real click nor a JS-dispatched click opens the form, and no alternative affordance exists. The partial-edit capability is simply absent.\n\n**IX-18 — Dashed dependency connections are unreachable by the mouse**\nThe hover handlers and tooltip content exist, but the SVG overlay carrying the connection paths is `pointer-events:none` at `z-index:0`, painted behind the task cards. `elementFromPoint` at the midpoint of all three connection paths returned task-card DIVs, never a path. Hovering the visible dashed stub produced no popup. Notably the same tooltip works from the warning badge (IX-20 passes), so this is a hit-testing/stacking defect rather than a missing feature.\n\n**CS-22 — Reopening a prerequisite creates an unrecoverable invalid state**\nThis is the most serious issue. With \"Complete tax filing\" depending on \"Review project proposal\" and both completed, reopening the prerequisite was permitted and the dependent was *not* returned to an incomplete state. The dependent now sits in the completed view (line-through, `state=\"completed\"`) while simultaneously displaying `Prerequisite \"Review project proposal\" incomplete` — exactly the contradiction the constraint forbids. Worse, both its complete toggle and edit button are disabled, so the user has no way to un-complete or edit it back to validity; deletion is the only escape.\n\nOne methodological note: the app holds all state in memory with no `localStorage`, so I verified persistence behavior directly and used a single deliberate reload (after confirming no data would be silently expected to survive) to clear a stuck tooltip before testing IX-18 in isolation — this ensured the tooltip I observed was attributable to the connection hover rather than a leftover from the earlier badge hover."
  }
}
